e Luria in a district with an even partisan lean. The midterm environment favors Democrats, and outside groups have poured roughly $2.7 million into ads opposing Kiggans, part of nearly $20 million in total television spending across the race. Both campaigns are well funded, with Luria raising slightly more than the incumbent, though Kiggans holds more cash on hand.\n\nEvery major race rater now calls the seat a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets give Luria about a 94 percent chance. A single recent poll shows Luria up three points among likely voters. The combined evidence points to a modest but meaningful Democratic edge, with Kiggans clinging to a narrow path if the national environment underperforms or local turnout breaks her way.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7923, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8055, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8023, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8046, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8169, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7631, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7572, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.798, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7517, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7695, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8458, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem